[h1]Smart Notifications[/h1]

Less notification noise, a watchlist for the countries you actually
care about, and new alerts — including one that names the exact law
worth enacting.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Key Features[/h1]

[list]
[b]Smarter notification defaults[/b] — a pass over vanilla's own
notification settings, demoting passive/low-value events (like transient
domestic political noise) from toast-tier to feed-tier, and quieting
repetitive dominion/subject diplomatic spam, without touching anything
you'd actually want a popup for.

[b]Relational country watchlist[/b] — flag the countries you actually
care about (rivals, allies, potential targets). Diplomatic plays, wars
starting, and countries joining a side now only interrupt you when a
watchlisted country (or you) is a genuine participant — not every play
happening anywhere in the world.

[b]Agitator Invite Available alert[/b] — fires when you have an open
agitator slot and an exiled character eligible to fill it, so the Invite
Exile opportunity doesn't quietly expire unnoticed.

[b]States with a Taxation Deficit alert[/b] — flags incorporated states
where tax collection can't keep up with spending, grouped into one
stacked entry when it's happening in more than one state.

[b]Law Ready to Enact alert[/b] — tick an opt-in checkbox on any law's
detail panel to mark it as one you're working toward. Once that law's
next checkpoint has better odds of succeeding than stalling, an alert
and a toast both name the exact law and its law group, so you know which
one to spend Political Power on.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]

[list]
[b]Save games:[/b] safe to add to an existing campaign at any time — it's
script/UI only, adds no new game mechanics. Removing it mid-campaign is
also expected to be safe (the mod's own tracked flags simply become
inert and are ignored, the way Jomini-engine mods generally handle
removed script content) but hasn't been stress-tested across many saves
yet — if you try it during the beta, please report back what you see.

[b]Achievements:[/b] unaffected. Steam achievements are disabled by
debug mode, not by having mods enabled — this mod doesn't touch that.

[b]Ironman:[/b] not applicable — Victoria 3 doesn't have an Ironman mode.

[b]Known conflicts:[/b] this mod fully replaces vanilla's
[i]common/messages/00_messages.txt[/i] (the file controlling default
notification presentation) to apply its notification-tuning pass. Any
other mod that [i]also[/i] fully replaces that same file will conflict —
whichever one loads later in your playset will silently win for every
setting in that file, not merge with the other. If you use another
notification-tuning or "QoL notification" mod, check for this specific
overlap. No other conflicts are known as of this beta.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Load Order Guidelines[/h1]

Load this mod after any general gameplay/content mods. If you use another
mod that changes default notification settings, load whichever one you
want to "win" for shared settings [b]last[/b] — see the Compatibility
note above on why they can't both apply their changes to the same file at
once. Otherwise, position doesn't matter — everything else this mod adds
(alerts, scripted triggers, the law-panel checkbox) is additive and
doesn't depend on load order relative to other mods.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Changelog[/h1]

[b]0.35 — initial private beta[/b]
[list]
[*] Agitator Invite Available alert
[*] States with a Taxation Deficit alert, plus a one-time toast naming
    the specific state
[*] Law Ready to Enact alert, with an opt-in per-law checkbox, plus a
    one-time toast naming the specific law and its law group
[*] (SN) tagging on all mod-added Message Settings rows and in-panel UI
    labels, so they're identifiable at a glance
[/list]

Full history of every change, including the notification-defaults pass
and the relational watchlist this beta builds on, is tracked in the
repository's own CHANGELOG.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Issue Reporting & Source[/h1]

This is a closed beta — thank you for testing. If you hit a bug or an
alert that doesn't behave as described above, please report it with:

[list]
[*] What you expected vs. what happened
[*] Your Victoria 3 version and any other mods enabled
[*] If possible, your [i]debug.log[/i] and [i]error.log[/i] from
    [i]Documents\Paradox Interactive\Victoria 3\logs\[/i] — this mod
    keeps detailed logging specifically so issues can be diagnosed from
    these files without needing a repro session
[/list]

Source and issue tracker: [url=https://github.com/dcoullon/victoria3-smart-notifications]github.com/dcoullon/victoria3-smart-notifications[/url]
